  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "We have only one data point (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), so the most critical uncertainty is whether adding image information (the core premise of a multimodal study) provides any benefit over the RNA-only baseline. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) differs from config_001 by exactly one design decision—adding image features via the simplest fusion (concat) and a standard encoder (resnet50). This makes it a clean, interpretable A/B comparison: if accuracy improves meaningfully over 48.5%, we confirm multimodal fusion is worthwhile and can then explore encoder/aggregation/fusion variants; if it does not, we redirect budget toward RNA-only improvements (better encoders, multiprofile). Testing multimodal first is more informative than testing image_only alone, because even weak image features can be complementary to RNA, and the direct comparison to our existing baseline isolates the fusion benefit. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design axis under a tight budget."
}

